Clean Harbors **Edmonton, AB** (with travel to **Fort McMurray, AB**) is seeking a Project **Operations Excellence Intern** to join our safety-focused Canadian Industrial Services team for **Summer 2027**. This internship provides a student with hands-on experience supporting operational excellence and project improvement initiatives across the **Canadian Industrial Services** organization.  

The intern will work alongside experienced operations and project leaders to analyze business processes, improve visibility to key performance indicators, document standard work, and support initiatives designed to improve operational consistency and execution. The successful candidate will own one or more defined business projects with measurable deliverables and present findings and recommendations to leadership at the conclusion of the internship.

This is a **full-time internship** and is **not eligible for remote work**. This position will require time in the field at customer and project sites.

**Start Dates:**

Start dates for our Summer 2027 Internship Program are **May 17th or May 24th, 2027**. Internships will run through the summer and end in August.  

**Why Intern with Clean Harbors?**  


* Health and Safety is our #1 priority and we live it 3-6-5!
* Clean Harbors offers students the opportunity to gain hands-on experience while working alongside professionals who are leading the way in environmental, energy, and industrial services.


**Our internship program is designed to provide:**  

* **Engagement** with teams, mentors, and leaders across the organization;
* **Experience** through meaningful projects that support real business priorities;
* **Education** about the environmental services industry and Clean Harbors operations;
* **Exposure** to career paths across operations, project management, analytics, engineering, and continuous improvement.

**Key Responsibilities**  

* Ensure Health and Safety is the number one priority by complying with all safe work practices, policies, and processes and acting safely at all times;
* Support operational excellence and continuous improvement projects across Canadian Industrial Services;
* Collect, organize, and analyze operational data to identify trends, gaps, and improvement opportunities;
* Assist in developing and maintaining dashboards, KPIs, scorecards, and recurring business reports;
* Map business and operational processes and recommend opportunities to improve efficiency, consistency, or visibility;
* Develop standard work, process documentation, project materials, and operating procedures;
* Support project planning through schedules, milestones, action trackers, meeting documentation, and status reporting;
* Partner with regional and functional leaders to understand operating practices and identify opportunities for standardization;
* Prepare executive-ready presentations and summaries communicating project findings and recommendations;
* Participate in field or operational exposure opportunities to understand how Industrial Services work is planned and executed;
* Complete a defined summer project and deliver a final leadership presentation summarizing outcomes, recommendations, and next steps.

**What Does It Take to Intern with Clean Harbors?**  

* Currently pursuing an undergraduate or graduate degree in **Engineering (EIT), Project Management (PMP), Business Administration** or **Business Management**, from an accredited college or university;
* Preference for a rising senior with anticipated graduation within approximately one year of completing the internship or recent graduates;
* Pursuing a degree in Industrial Engineering, Operations Management, Business Administration, Project Management, Supply Chain, Business Analytics, Engineering, or a related discipline;
* Strong analytical, problem-solving, and critical-thinking skills;
* Ability to work with data and translate analysis into practical business recommendations;
* Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint; experience with Power BI or another data-visualization tool is an asset;
* Strong written and verbal communication skills;
* Ability to organize multiple priorities, follow through on commitments, and work with limited supervision;
* Interest in process improvement, continuous improvement, project management, and industrial operations;
* Ability to collaborate with operational leaders and employees across different locations and functions;
* Willingness to spend time in office and industrial operating environments and travel to field locations as needed.

**Illustrative Summer Project**  
Canadian Industrial Services Operational Excellence and KPI Standardization  
The intern may evaluate how selected operational KPIs and processes are tracked across Canadian Industrial Services groups, identify inconsistencies or improvement opportunities, and recommend a more standardized approach. Potential deliverables include:  

* A current-state assessment of selected processes and KPIs;
* Process maps identifying gaps, handoffs, or inconsistent practices;
* A KPI or dashboard prototype that improves leadership visibility;
* Standard-work recommendations that can be applied across multiple regions;
* An implementation roadmap identifying priorities, owners, and practical next steps;
* A final leadership presentation summarizing findings and business opportunities.

**Want to Learn More About Starting Your Career with Clean Harbors?**  
As a Clean Harbors intern, you will gain hands-on experience working alongside field teams and operational leaders who support environmental and industrial services across North America. Your internship may include time at a facility or project site, participation in safety briefings, observation of operational processes, and exposure to how teams safely manage complex environmental and industrial work.  
